 communities within the region are  already doing  how to start our own sustainable journey  energy journey and how to access the  support available to local parishes  we hope you come away from today's  events knowing your bright ideas can  become a reality  babe mid-suffolk district councils have  stated our commitment for suffolk to be  carbon neutral and to continue down the  path of sustainability  this is not a one-time fix and then  return to the old ways  those ways are behind us now  going forward we will all be taking  great steps to make our homes a reality  your attendance here today has proved  that reducing the impact of climate  change is an important issue for  communities right now  we are incredibly grateful to everyone  here who is doing their very best to  embrace new energy solutions to move  towards a brighter greener future  before i wrap up i would like to give a  very big shout out to everyone who made  today possible particularly the baba mid  suffolk teams  and a big thank you to all of you all  thank you very much  [Applause]  i hope like me you have been energized  by what you have heard today  dan and tom's comments really resonated  with me and i'm very pleased that we at  baby mitzvah have adopted strategies to  address some of these issues  so let's turn today's knowledge into  practical solutions and take a leap  towards our new carbon neutral lives  we will be gathering feedback so we can  come back next time with an even bigger  and better event so we can learn from  each other from the work that we would  have done in the meantime  and by the way also a recording of this  event will be available on our youtube  channel in due course  so once again thank you all and have a  lovely weekend  [Applause]  you

